# SaveVideoKit — public video / audio download & inspect

Use the `savevideokit` MCP server to download or inspect public videos/audio. No API key required.

## Download policy — mandatory

**Direct first. Relay only when a merge is physically required.**

```
inspect_video(url)
├─ direct_options non-empty  ──►  DIRECT: fetch direct_options[].download_url (302 → source CDN)
└─ direct_options empty      ──►  RELAY: create_download → poll → save
```

- **DIRECT** is the default whenever it is offered: the URL redirects to the original media file, so nothing is downloaded, merged or stored by the service — no job, no polling, no retention race.
- **RELAY** only when no complete single file exists: `direct_download_available == false`, `direct_options == []`, every `formats[].direct_eligible == false`, or reasons such as `requires_headers` (CDN tied to the page Referer/UA, e.g. TikTok) and `not_mp4` (audio-only / incompatible container). That is the "a merge is needed" case.
- Never call `create_download` before reading the direct fields. Never relay "because the user wants an mp4" — a direct option already is a playable mp4. Never poll after a direct fetch.

## Tools
- `inspect_video({url})` → metadata, formats, plus `direct_download_available` and `direct_options[]` (`{download_url, ext, resolution, width, height, filesize}`)
- `create_download({url, format?, quality?})` → `job_id` (relay only)
- `get_download_status({job_id})` → `{status, progress, download_url}`; generated files are kept 30 minutes
- `get_supported_sites({})` → service/engine version + 32 verified / 33 featured / 1735 sites

## Workflow
1. `inspect_video` first. Read the title and the direct fields.
2. If `direct_options` is non-empty → fetch the best option (highest `height` within the quality cap) right away:
   `scripts/download_file.py "<download_url>" "<dir>" --name "<title>" --ext "<option.ext>" --referer "<webpage_url>"`
3. Only if `direct_options` is empty → `create_download({url, format: "mp4"})`, parse `job_id`, poll `get_download_status` every ~5s until `success` / `failed` / `expired`, then save `download_url` with the same script.
4. Always save under the video title (never a random id); the MCP only returns a URL and never writes to disk.
5. Verify the file exists and size > 0, and say whether it came direct or from a server-side merge.

## Limits
- Public content only; no private/age-restricted/region-locked; no watermark removal; no playlists/batch.
- No platform gate: any public URL can be attempted.
- Direct link `403`/`404` → the signed option expired: re-run `inspect_video`, do not downgrade to relay.
- A relay `download_url` expires after ~30 minutes; then create a new `create_download` task.

See `references/constraints.md` for details.

## Keeping up to date

On first activation in a session, check for a newer release and auto-update the SaveVideoKit skill/rule:

```
python3 cursor/scripts/check_update.py --auto
```

This compares `VERSION` with the latest GitHub release of SaveVideoKit/mcp (cached 24h) and updates the `cursor/` folder in place when a newer release exists, keeping a `<dir>.bak-<timestamp>` backup. Use `--check` to only report, `--force` to bypass the cache.
